From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd, virgl: tiled resources (tier 2), min/max filtering

Direct3D 11.2's tiled resources on the host's sparse storage (WinBoat's virglrenderer 0021-0023):
- Tiled.cpp: MISC_TILED resources are sparse (PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_SPARSE: virgl's VIRGL_BIND_SPARSE), MISC_TILE_POOL
  ones memory only (PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_TILE_POOL: VIRGL_BIND_TILE_POOL), in chunks so ResizeTilePool keeps the tiles
  it had. Tiles have D3D's standard shapes (the host's sparse pages have them); mips smaller than a tile in either
  dimension are packed (the host's mip tail), one tile per slice. UpdateTileMappings, CopyTileMappings (every tile's
  mapping is kept), CopyTiles, UpdateTiles, TiledResourceBarrier, GetMipPacking, ResizeTilePool, the TILED format
  support, single-sampled tiled quality levels. A new pipe_context hook, tile_map, binds a region to a pool's memory
  at an offset (virgl: VIRGL_CCMD_TILE_MAP). Tiled textures transfer through staging buffers; tiled buffers and pools
  have no guest storage (GPU copies; UpdateSubresource on a tiled buffer through a staging buffer). virgl reads a
  sparse resource back on every map: an aliased tile changes behind it.
- Tier 2: unmapped tiles read 0 (the host's sparse_texture2); the feedback variants of sample/gather/ld and
  check_access_fully_mapped (ShaderTGSI.c's translate_feedback: the base instruction with a TGSI SPARSE before its
  texture instruction, which the host turns into the lookup's residency and LOD clamp; the status 1 or 0); min/max
  filtering (the sampler filter's reduction type, bits 7-8, as gallium's reduction_mode: virgl's sampler S0 bits
  26-27 where the host takes them; MAXIMUM_* filters were taken for comparison ones before, by their 0x80 bit).
- With tier 1 the runtime gives ClearView on depth-only formats: ClearView on depth-stencil views clears the depth.
D3DWDDM1_3DDICAPS_D3D11_OPTIONS1 reports tier 1 where the host announces VIRGL_CAP_V2_TILED, tier 2 with
VIRGL_CAP_V2_SAMPLER_REDUCTION and VIRGL_CAP_V2_SPARSE_FEEDBACK too.
---
